            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the infiltration test we notice air leakage coming from the windows, doors, attic hatch, furnace air supply and the doors.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>According to the measure on site, we estimate the level of insulation of the exterior walls to be R-20 which is under the actual standard of R-28. We recommend the addition of R-20 to be eligible to the rebate of 2.50$/square foot. This addition will increase the level of insulation at R-40.



We recommend to proceed on the exterior part of the wall. This way will help to increase the air tightness of the building and insure a better performance of the building envelope.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>The actual level of insulation of the attic is R-40. We recommend the addition of insulation to reach a level of R-60 or even R-70.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <windows>The actual windows are wood frame and some of the the wood is damaged. We recommend the replacement of all windows with ENERGY STAR certified windows suitable for ZONE 3.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the doors by ENERGY STAR certified doors.</doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
